2. Introduction
This report documents the security assessment activities completed during Week 2 of the Networkwalks Cybersecurity Internship Program. It covers two foundational phases of reconnaissance: footprinting the networkwalks.com domain using Kali Linux utilities (W2-PM1) and performing host discovery on a local network environment using Zenmap (W2-PM5).

Together, these modules illustrate the initial reconnaissance stages of the cyber kill chain, demonstrating how an assessor transitions from gathering public intelligence to actively mapping live infrastructure on a target network. All commands and procedures were executed within controlled environments utilizing Kali Linux and a Windows workstation. To maintain rigorous documentation standards, each subsection within this report includes:

